@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' SPEC: _spec/_plans/chess-ui-primitives.puml
' status: PROPOSED — goals and contracts, not shipped behavior
' scope: Android portability, shared analytics, maintainer handoff
' covers: none — proposed contracts; source coverage starts at implementation
 title PLANNED — Android alternatives and centralized player analytics

package "Existing product boundaries" {
  component "apps/ui — /chess\nCoach primitive kit" as COACH <<app>>
  component "apps/starchess — /starchess\nStarChess primitive kit" as STAR <<app>>
}

note bottom of COACH
  **1. Enable native Android alternatives**
  Keep each product's presentation kit.
  Extract state / command contracts where needed.
  Keep browser APIs behind platform adapters.
  Do not create a third visual design system.
end note

note bottom of STAR
  **Existing footholds**
  StarChess: src/ports and adapters/browser.
  packages/client-platform: device detection.
  engine-core and starchess-core: audit reuse.
  These do not establish Android compatibility.
end note

package "Proposed boundaries — implementation pending" {
  component "Android presentation alternatives\n/chess and /starchess equivalents" as ANDROID <<app>>
  component "Shared analytics contract\nproduct adapters + privacy gate" as EVENTS <<app>>
  component "Delivery adapters\nweb beacon / native HTTP" as SEND <<async>>
  component "Serverless collector\nprovider TBD" as COLLECT <<app>>
  database "Bounded aggregate + dedup state\nTTL and hard capacity limit" as STATE <<db>>
  component "Scheduled digest\nfixed maintainer recipient" as DIGEST <<async>>
  cloud "Transactional email provider\nprovider TBD" as EMAIL <<cloud>>
  actor "Maintainer" as OWNER
}

COACH ARROW_OPTIONAL EVENTS : proposed instrumentation
STAR ARROW_OPTIONAL EVENTS : proposed instrumentation
ANDROID ARROW_OPTIONAL EVENTS : same event semantics
EVENTS ARROW_QUEUE SEND : permitted events only
SEND ARROW_QUEUE COLLECT : bounded HTTPS batches
COLLECT ARROW_MAIN STATE : validate / deduplicate / aggregate
STATE ARROW_OPTIONAL DIGEST : scheduled summary
DIGEST ARROW_CLOUD EMAIL : capped digest delivery
EMAIL ARROW_CLOUD OWNER : player activity summary

note left of ANDROID
  **Android direction: native screens**
  Share serializable domain contracts.
  Preserve each product's rules and identity.
  Spike TS runtime / bridge or domain port first.
  Prove one playable flow in each product.
end note

note right of EVENTS
  **2. Standardize analytics**
  schemaVersion + event-name allowlist.
  eventId, product, platform, appVersion, time.
  Allowlisted per-event payload; shared meanings.
  Initial events: session start, match finished.
end note

note left of EVENTS
  Use product-owned persisted match outcomes.
  Do not re-score games or equate result enums.
  Keep product-specific payloads namespaced.
  chess-analytics.puml owns local read models.
  This plan owns collection and maintainer use.
end note

note bottom of EVENTS
  Proposed default: collection disabled.
  Opt-in controls all transports; revoke clears queue.
  No names, email, board dumps or raw URLs.
  No persistent player ID or fingerprint.
  Session counts do not mean unique players.
end note

note left of SEND
  Never block play; cap queue, age and batch size.
  Beacon acceptance does not prove delivery.
  Native uses HTTP, not navigator.sendBeacon.
  Bound retry attempts; drop expired events.
  Suspend / exit may lose unsent events.
end note

note right of COLLECT
  Treat every client payload as untrusted.
  Enforce schema, bytes, rates and global quotas.
  CORS is not authentication or abuse prevention.
  Keep email credentials only on the server.
  Drop excess traffic; never activate paid fallback.
end note

note right of STATE
  Deduplicate eventId within a bounded TTL.
  Expire raw identifiers after aggregation.
  Set retention and capacity before deployment.
  Avoid payload / IP logging in app and provider.
  Acceptance does not guarantee digest inclusion.
end note

note bottom of DIGEST
  **3. Draft player-to-maintainer handoff**
  Summarize product, version, event and outcome.
  Send a capped digest, not one email per event.
  Escape content; clients cannot select recipients.
  Bound retries; duplicate / lost mail is possible.
end note

note bottom of EMAIL
  **Zero cost is an unverified research target**
  Verify ingest, storage, scheduler, email quotas.
  Check sender/domain prerequisites and abuse costs.
  Define volume budget and stop-at-limit behavior.
  Select providers only after feasibility research.
end note

legend bottom
  **Implementation sequence and verification gates — planned**
  1. Inventory browser coupling in both products; spike Android runtime choices.
     Gate: playable start / move / finish flow for each product on Android.
  2. Define portable commands, state and analytics schema; add product adapters.
     Gate: shared fixtures for results; reject unknown versions and payload fields.
  3. Add opt-in web / native delivery adapters with bounded buffering.
     Gate: disabled / revoked collection, offline, duplicate, overflow and exit cases.
  4. Research zero-cost providers; implement collector, aggregation and digest.
     Gate: malformed traffic, abuse quotas, TTL, email failures and fixed recipient.
  5. Persist unit / integration / web E2E and Android smoke coverage before rollout.
     Run affected typecheck / lint and StarChess check:css-layout for UI changes.
     Link implementing source and tests to this plan when those files exist.
  **Open decisions:** native runtime integration; providers; numeric quotas / TTL / digest cadence.
  **Scope now:** plan update only; no deployment, credentials or analytics collection.
end legend
@enduml
